  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The analysis is limited to a qualitative thematic tracking of six selected indexes, which may not capture the full diversity of localized or informal smart city metrics used by individual municipalities.",
      "what": "This study tracks the conceptual evolution of smart city evaluation frameworks between 2017 and 2022. The researchers conducted a longitudinal thematic analysis of six prominent smart city indexes, selected from an initial inventory of sixteen frameworks.",
      "why": "It documents a structural shift in how urban smartness is defined and measured, showing that evaluation frameworks have transitioned from purely technocentric metrics toward integrated logics that incorporate governance capacity, economic conditions, and societal dimensions."
    }
